#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186383851 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "09d8ec89-4d75-51ac-a870-1d2f8a1800ba" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Matrix Left Multiplication Equivalent To a Given Row Operation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "76e1d450-b3ef-57af-9c64-ab8be1886d53" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383853} {:answer/id #uuid "c7229ed6-7988-530d-a977-60c39c21da12" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383854} {:answer/id #uuid "c74b1327-57a3-5079-9810-08cee14b8c4f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383855} {:answer/id #uuid "e8acb90f-f0ff-5180-b4c9-3f2ce56526ea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383856} {:answer/id #uuid "4a9a90e1-5dba-5ab0-9ee2-104f8632a37f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383857}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4a9a90e1-5dba-5ab0-9ee2-104f8632a37f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383857} :answer-field/id #uuid "d1c3165d-bd53-5d9a-a729-a417d9b41a88" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383852}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c63ff4bb-da6b-5999-bbc7-816dc82a29a6" :question/math-academy-id "q-110471" :question/problem "Suppose that the elementary row operation \n${R}_{2}:=3{R}_{2}$ is applied to a $3\\times 3$ matrix $A.$ What is the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication?" :question/worked-solution "We need to find a matrix $E$ such that $EA$ is equivalent to applying the elementary row operation ${R}_{2}:=3{R}_{2}$ to $A.$\n\nTo find $E,$ we apply the given row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=3{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =E\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication is $EA:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186383858 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "00b69189-1ae1-5625-adfb-e5460845c776" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Matrix Left Multiplication Equivalent To a Sequence of Row Operations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "de3c6e94-f543-5c16-98f0-1e3146f7eff8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383860} {:answer/id #uuid "c8e61017-63c1-5e69-9922-3c3eea3a6b3f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383861} {:answer/id #uuid "53bc419f-611d-5b57-a773-9650534b20d1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383862} {:answer/id #uuid "ca300e7e-9d7a-53b6-8c3e-72568609817e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383863} {:answer/id #uuid "79e6fec9-212a-5eaf-973f-1ef5080c6860" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -6 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383864}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ca300e7e-9d7a-53b6-8c3e-72568609817e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383863} :answer-field/id #uuid "fe03e7ec-d1e6-5682-8944-61e7a8fa8b03" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383859}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "324f3608-babb-59d3-b059-1a5e8e0a8c0c" :question/math-academy-id "q-32133" :question/problem "Suppose that the following elementary row operations are applied to a $3\\times 3$ matrix $A$ in the given order:\n\n$$\n{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}-2{R}_{2},\\,{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}-3{R}_{1}\n$$\n\nWhat is the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication?" :question/worked-solution "First, let's find the elementary matrices corresponding to the given elementary row operations.\n\n- The first operation is ${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}-2{R}_{2}.$ The corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}-2{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={E}_{1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The second operation is ${R}_{3}:={R}_{3}-3{R}_{1}.$ The corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={E}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo apply the first elementary row operation to the matrix $A,$ we multiply by ${E}_{1}$ on the left and get ${E}_{1}A:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A\n$$\n\nThen, to apply the second elementary row operation to ${E}_{1}A,$ we multiply by ${E}_{2}$ on the left and get ${E}_{2}{E}_{1}A:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186383865 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "09d8ec89-4d75-51ac-a870-1d2f8a1800ba" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Matrix Left Multiplication Equivalent To a Given Row Operation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1854bec2-cf1a-5ba4-a46a-ce3506dcbe0c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "A\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -\\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383867} {:answer/id #uuid "fa7b5670-0364-5c37-9421-f7307e045b0e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -\\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383868} {:answer/id #uuid "0f18f460-1c27-5557-8873-b95a771f0